# QuikTransit — Next.js App

On-demand ride and package delivery app built with Next.js 14, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS.

## Project Structure

```
quiktransit/
├── app/
│   ├── page.tsx              ← Home screen (choose Customer or Driver)
│   ├── customer/
│   │   ├── layout.tsx
│   │   └── page.tsx          ← Customer booking app
│   └── driver/
│       ├── layout.tsx
│       └── page.tsx          ← Driver dashboard
├── components/
│   └── shared/
│       ├── TopBar.tsx        ← Orange header bar
│       ├── MapView.tsx       ← OpenStreetMap embed
│       └── AddressInput.tsx  ← Google Places autocomplete input
├── lib/
│   ├── constants.ts          ← Pricing, payment info, types, helpers
│   └── maps.ts               ← Google Maps loader + Distance Matrix
├── .env.local                ← Your API keys and business info
└── README.md
```

## Quick Start

1. Install dependencies:
   ```bash
   npm install
   ```

2. Add your Google Maps API key to `.env.local`:
   ```
   NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY=AIzaSy...
   ```
   Get a free key at https://console.cloud.google.com
   Enable: Maps JavaScript API, Places API, Distance Matrix API

3. Update your payment handles in `.env.local`:
   ```
   NEXT_PUBLIC_PAYPAL=rmusil2@gmail.com
   NEXT_PUBLIC_PHONE=714-292-1804
   ```

4. Run the dev server:
   ```bash
   npm run dev
   ```
   Open http://localhost:3000

## Pages

| URL | Description |
|-----|-------------|
| `/` | Home — choose Customer or Driver |
| `/customer` | Customer booking flow with map, payments, tips |
| `/driver` | Driver dashboard with requests, tracking, earnings |

## Deploy to Namecheap

1. Build: `npm run build`
2. The output is in `.next/` — Namecheap shared hosting doesn't support Node.js servers natively.
3. **Recommended:** Deploy to [Vercel](https://vercel.com) (free tier, made by Next.js team):
   - Push to GitHub → connect Vercel → auto-deploys on every push
   - Add env vars in Vercel dashboard
4. Point your Namecheap domain DNS to Vercel (they have a guide at vercel.com/docs/projects/domains)

## Customizing Pricing

Edit `NEXT_PUBLIC_RATE_PER_MILE` in `.env.local`. The `calcFare()` function in `lib/constants.ts` handles all fare math automatically.

